2. Everything else — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
------------------------------------

All the non-software material — the prompts, the model responses under `data/`,
the CLDW-derived data, and the generated figures and tables in `reports/` — is
licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
International Licence (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), the same licence as the original
Corpus of Lake District Writing (CLDW) on which it draws.

    Deed:       http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
    Legal code: http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

You are free to share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes,
provided you give appropriate credit and distribute your contributions under
the same licence.

Suggested attribution:

    Blackwell, R., Taylor, J. E., Rayson, P., Gregory, I. N., Ezeani, I., &
    Cohn, N. "Can AI Build (Better) Literary Corpora? Preliminary lessons from
    the Corpus of Lake District Writing." Journal of Open Humanities Data.

The CLDW is published by UCREL at Lancaster University
(https://github.com/UCREL/LakeDistrictCorpus). As its creators request, work
using it should also cite:

    Rayson, P., Reinhold, A., Butler, J., Donaldson, C. E., Gregory, I. N., &
    Taylor, J. E. (2017). A deeply annotated testbed for geographical text
    analysis: The Corpus of Lake District Writing.
    https://doi.org/10.1145/3149858.3149865

